    s__HEARTBURN_PREGNANT(py_str("Heartburn is very common in pregnancy and eases once the baby is born: the hormones relax the valve at the top of the stomach, and later the baby takes the room. Eat little and often, stay upright an hour after eating, prop the head of the bed up 10 to 15cm, and try an antacid or an alginate (Gaviscon and the like) - ask a pharmacist or your midwife before omeprazole. Tell your midwife if it stops you eating or sleeping."));
